---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Subscribe from "../components/forms/Subscribe.astro";
---

<Base>
  <article class="flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-12 px-8 py-10 text-xl leading-snug text-pretty md:px-9 md:text-2xl [&_h2]:border-b [&_h2]:border-ink [&_h2]:pb-2 [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h3]:mt-2 [&_h3]:font-semibold [&>section]:flex [&>section]:flex-col [&>section]:gap-6">
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h1 class="text-4xl leading-tight font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-5xl">40 for 40</h1>
      <p>The joy of just <strong class="font-semibold">making stuff</strong> again.</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Anyone else feeling this?</h2>
      <p>Twenty minutes ago, you felt unstoppable. You’d just built something you couldn’t have made a year ago. You didn’t even type. You Wispr’d it like Al Capone in a smoky jazz club.</p>
      <p class="font-semibold italic">Hell yes!</p>
      <p>Let’s go on LinkedIn and show everyone my… then it hits you.</p>
      <p class="font-semibold italic">Oh shit.</p>
      <p>A teenager’s built an algo arbitrage bot on Kalshi making $36k/mo. At this rate, they’ll be podcasting on 20VC before I’ve finished my… OMG, did he just raise a $50 million Seed round?</p>
      <p>How does that make sense?</p>
      <p>That’s what the world feels like right now.</p>
      <p>40 for 40 is the counterweight to all of this uncertainty.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <ul class="flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 pl-6">
        <li><strong class="font-semibold">40 apps in 40 days:</strong> like a hackathon in public</li>
        <li><strong class="font-semibold">Live:</strong> Streamed on Twitch, daily shorts on socials</li>
        <li><strong class="font-semibold">How to participate:</strong> Watch, Interact, or Build with us. Heck, if you want to come down to our studio, let’s make that happen.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This is a community and we’re going to bring the fun back to building</p>
      <p class="font-semibold italic">November 2, 2026 - 40 for 40 begins.</p>
    </section>
